# Every path in this repository is owned by the maintainer.
#
# Paired with `require_code_owner_review` on the "main: require pull request"
# ruleset, this makes @TerryOtt's approval mandatory on every pull request to
# main — not merely "one approval from somebody with write access", which is
# what a bare review count would mean once there is more than one collaborator.
#
# Two consequences worth knowing:
#
#   - A code owner cannot approve their own pull request. That never bites here,
#     because the maintainer bypasses the pull-request ruleset entirely and
#     commits straight to main; see docs/REVIEWING.md.
#   - A code owner must have write access to the repository, or the rule silently
#     matches nobody. Check that before adding anyone to this file.

